\par\par \b \uc2  S Korean Kospi Opens 4.1% Up On Nasdaq, \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2001\par 02:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SEOUL -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main stock index opened significantly higher Friday on Nasdaq's surge overnight and Bank of Korea's announcement it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At 0008 GMT (8:08 p.m. EDT Thursday), the Korea Composite Stock Price Index rose 20.22, or 4.1%, to 513.91, on volume of 58.5 million shares valued at 206.4 billion won ($1=KRW1,365.2). Decliners led gainers 595 to 218 with 53 stocks unchanged. Seventeen stocks were up by the 15% daily limit, while 30 stocks were limit-down 15%. \par \par \uc2  Nasdaq soared 8.9% Wednesday as Dell Computer Corp. offered positive earnings projection and Alcoa Inc. reported strong earnings. \par \par \uc2  Also boosting domestic sentiment was the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's approval of measures to dip into its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve of $94.4 billion to prop up the sagging won. The won opened up stronger against the dollar Friday morning, at 1,340 against Wednesday's close of 1,365.2. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy meeting Friday is unlikely to affect the financial markets, traders said, because there is no hope the bank will cut interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Blue-chip stocks are higher Friday. Pohang Iron & Steel Co. is up 3.2%, or KRW2,900, at KRW93,900. Korea Electric Power Corp. has risen 6.7%, or KRW1,250, to KRW19,850. SK Telecom Co. has gained 7.3%, or KRW12,000, to KRW177,000. Daishin Securities Co. has added 8.8%, or KRW850, to KRW10,550. Samsung Electronics Co. is up 5.5%, or KRW10,000, to KRW193,000. \par \par \uc2  Foreigners were net buyers of KRW27.8 billion worth of shares, financial institutions were net sellers of KRW36.4 billion worth of shares, and retail investors were net buyers of KRW12.3 billion worth of shares. \par \par \uc2  -Seoul Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-732-2156 \par \par \uc2  5029 55112 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx4601io4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
