\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  dealers in Korea to curb speculative trading. \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2000\par 04:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Aug 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers at major banks in South Korea, including foreign banks, plan to hold off on speculative trading to protest against government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a move which would severely curtail liquidity, industry sources said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said halting such trade would erase about 80 percent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's trade volume. \par \par \uc2  "The government's excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stifles the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said a local bank dealer. "It also severely undermines corporate awareness about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said recent trade has been held to a tight range by what they dubbed "government-instructed" importer and exporter settlements. \par \par \uc2  About 30 dealers met on Thursday and agreed to stop speculative trading, limiting themselves to commercial orders. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea official said trading volume fell to about $1.2 billion on Thursday, from the current daily average of $2 billion. \par \par \uc2  Officials at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy denied \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by directing action by state-run banks or others. \par \par \uc2  "Dealers seem to have taken this action because the current tight range of trade means little opportunity for profits," said Joo Hwan-wook, deputy director of the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy division. \par \par \uc2  "We are not doing the things the dealers accuse us of," Joo said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the International Monetary Fund said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  should limit \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  The won has appreciated about 1.8 percent since the close of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The won -2 fell slightly to 1,114.3 per dollar by 0111 GMT against Thursday's close of 1,114.1. \par \par \uc2  It opened at 1,113.9 and moved between 1,113.9 and 1,114.3. \par \par \uc2  The dollar/won rate was forecast to range from 1,113 to 1,115 won on Friday. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw8p0aila\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
