\par\par \b \uc2  Korea's c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mkt to buy dlrs. \b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2000\par 08:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to slow the pace of the won's rise against the dollar, a bank official said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The official, who refused to be identified, said the bank has purchased dollars through state-run banks to help check the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising too quickly. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the won rose to 1,117.6 in mid-afternoon trade, boosted by heavy foreign buying of local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market saw about $200 million in dollar demand from state banks. \par \par \uc2  The won dropped to 1,118.8 by 0630 GMT after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It opened at 1,125.0 compared with Friday's close of 1,125.2. \par \par \uc2  ((Nam In-soo +82 2 727-5644, fax +82 2 727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw650443i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
