\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Pressured by dollar bulls. \b0\par\par\uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2000\par 04:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 4 (Reuters) - Asian regionals \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  edged lower in early trade on Thursday, weighed by the dollar's \par \par \uc2  strength which holds despite Wall Street's slip. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said market participants rushed to cover any short \par \par \uc2  dollar positions versus regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the dollar's \par \par \uc2  broad-based gains against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The sickly euro\tab     was hovering near its record low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 88.87 cents overnight and dealers said there was little to stop\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it extending the slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the fact that the euro failed to capitalise on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the recent volatility in the U.S. equity markets had led to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further disenchantment among long-term investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. unit broke above 109 yen\tab     in muted trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due to the Golden Week holidays in Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won edged lower against the dollar in early trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite a strong rise in the KOSDAQ.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Investors were reluctant to push it higher due to fears of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the weaker yen, dealers said. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Japan compete in similar export markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Finance Ministry on Wednesday issued a verbal warning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to rein in the won. The move was following by state-run banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par absorbing dollars from the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Seoul said they expected the won to trade in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range of 1,109 to 1,112 won for the rest of the session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah is expected to move in a narrow range after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market had discounted the news that the letter of intent to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par IMF might be signed soon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The agreement will allow Jakarta to tap a long-delayed loan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth $400 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers expected the unit to trade in a 7,950-8,000 range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Thursday. A fall below 8,020 is expected to trigger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dollar bids from offshore players continued to keep the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par baht on the defensive, although sporadic profit-taking helped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it gain some ground.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers see a strong support for the baht at 38.50 where\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exporter offers are lined up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Swap rates in the offshore market have risen sharply due to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tight baht liquidity as players held on to dollars. One-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/baht offshore forward rate rose to 5/7 satang from 1/3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par satang early on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso nudged up in early Asian trading, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wariness over further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tightly fixed in a range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Everybody is expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in, so\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par we're not going to see much activity," one dealer at a major\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars on Wednesday to curb the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decline of the peso around 41.28 in the face of general\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakness in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market players expected the peso to trade between 41.20 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 41.28 per dollar on Thursday with 41.40 in sight if it broke\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through the bottom of that range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar opened Thursday's trade at 30.69,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly firmer than Wednesday's close of 30.693.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers said the wider picture was of downward pressure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on the Taiwan dollar in the face of a weakening yen and a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent poor stock market performance.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers also said uncertainty surrounding Taiwan and China\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par added to pressure on the Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan's Finance Minister Paul Chiu on Thursday called for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence in the stock market, saying the island's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fundamentals are strong and pledged to take "necessary"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par measures to stabilise the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Turnover through dealers on the main market was heavy at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$155 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar gained momentum to rise above the key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.72 level while the market remained cautious of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The very weak euro, yen and higher U.S. dollar against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par other regionals suggest that we are some way from the zone\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par where authorities might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , despite the recent dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upside," Bank of America said in its daily market review.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market was driven mostly by profit-taking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with 1.7250 eyed as the crucial level for the Sing dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0939 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     109.23\tab  108.85\tab    -0.35\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7190\tab  1.7187\tab    -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    30.690\tab  30.693\tab    +0.01\par  Korean won   1110.70\tab 1109.80\tab    -0.08\p