\par\par \b \uc2  Korea won ends little changed after tight trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\tab     -2 closed marginally lower on Friday after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by monetary authorities thwarted dollar-unwinding by long-position holders, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won closed at 1,117.3 per dollar against Thursday's close of 1,117.2. It opened at a low of 1,118.5 and touched a high of 1,117.2.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "The market is long in dollars due to steady foreign buying of local stocks," said a foreign bank dealer. "But because of the government's dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the trading is stuck in a tight range." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy said before the market opened it was concerned about the won's appreciation against the dollar though the level of foreign buying of local stocks had recently fallen. \par \par \uc2  The ministry reiterated its pledge to take action whenever necessary to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. \par \par \uc2  Actual dollar buying by state-run banks followed the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the opening bell. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today was estimated at about $150 million, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Net foreign stock buying was about 176 billion won on Friday, on top of 123.5 billion on Thursday, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the yen's fall against the dollar also helped curb the won's upside. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen\tab   was at 105.97/98 at 0822 GMT against 105.46/49 late in Tokyo on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers forecast the dollar/won rate would range from 1,115 to 1,120 on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Offshore dollar/won trading was thin as spot trading was stuck in a narrow range, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The six-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) won was quoted at 1,117.8/19.3 against 1,117.5/19.5 late on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The one-year won stood at 1,119.5/23.0 against 1,119.0/21.0.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Kim Myong-hwan, +822 727 5645, fax 822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3h04g5w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
