\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Yen meddling sours regional mood. \b0\par\par\uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, March 15 (Reuters) - Heavy yen\tab \par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) weighed on regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Wednesday despite a brief respite for the \par \par \uc2  baht and peso. \par \par \uc2      The baht and peso edged higher after Thailand's bankrupcy \par \par \uc2  court ruled in favour of creditors in a landmark case involving \par \par \uc2  Thailand's biggest debt defaulter, Thai Petrochemical Industry \par \par \uc2  (TPI)   . \par \par \uc2      In the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the spotlight trailed on \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen after it jumped more than one percent to a high of \par \par \uc2  105.75 on the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a week ago, selling yen \par \par \uc2  for dollars to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has \par \par \uc2  appreciated 6.4 percent against the dollar since February 22 \par \par \uc2  amid optimism over Japan's recovery. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro\tab     was steady against the dollar and at the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par top of its intraday range against the yen following the BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht soon surrendered a 0.2 percent gain, sparked by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par news of that Thailand's Bankruptcy Court had found TPI\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par insolvent and ordered it to be restructured.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The court also ruled that TPI's chief executive officer be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the interim planner for the company while creditors met to pick\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their own planner to revamp the company.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts had expected a ruling in favour of TPI to hurt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai markets and investor perception of the government's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commitment to bankruptcy reform.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht's rise was thwarted by confusion over whether\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Chatu Mongol Sonakul had threatened to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resign due to a bitter dispute with the cabinet.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A cabinet source told Reuters Chatu had said he would step\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down if proposed changes to the Bank of Thailand (BOT) Act were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par approved without alterations ensuring the bank's independence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But the director of the BOT's legal department later denied\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that Chatu had threatened to quit.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON\tab      -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won was off intraday highs of 1,115 per dollar after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen was swiped off recent peaks, calming fears of won\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Korean authorities.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Economy said it was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ready to take action to cap the won's rise against the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and that it was not desirable for the won to appreciate in line\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the market had been reluctant to sell dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par below 1,116/1,117 on Wednesday and that range-trading was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A Reuters poll showed that South Korean GDP was expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par grow 6.8 percent in 2000 and 6.0 percent in 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah slipped in line with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after trading in a tight 7,390-7,440 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah market has come under slight pressure recently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par amid worries the International Monetary Fund might again\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suspend its loan programme to the country if key players in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Bali  banking scandal are not brought to justice.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Though the IMF warned lending might be halted the previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day, Jakarta dealers expressed confidence the matter would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resolved.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesian GDP was seen rising 3.86 percent in 2000 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 4.95 percent in 2001, according to a Reuters poll.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso was off an intraday high of around 40.7 seen after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht steadied on the back of the TPI court ruling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But sentiment remained weak due to concerns over likely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. rate hikes, a domestic stock manipulation scandal linked\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to gaming and leisure firm BW Resource Corp  and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regional uncertainties like presidential elections in Taiwan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Philippine GDP was forecast to grow 3.66 percent in 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 4.05 percent in 2001, according to a Reuters poll.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar slid back through the 1.71 support as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen slid in the wake of the BOJ's dollar buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     With few domestic leads to trade on, analysts said the Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar was taking its cue from the yen and technical factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The U.S. dollar looked well supported at S$1.7028 for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par time being, SEB Merchant Banking said in a daily report.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar kept its grip despite hefty stock market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses as pre-election jitters and the U.S. Nasdaq's four\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent overnight drop weighed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Fears a pro-independence candidate might win Saturday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presidential poll continued to discourage investors, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's downside was being cushioned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Taipei dealers said the bank had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  actively in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past two sessions, clearly signalling its desire for exchange\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate stability.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0849 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.88\tab  104.78\tab    -1.04\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7123\tab  1.7066\tab    -0.33\par  Taiwan dlr    30.742\tab  30.738\tab    -0.01\par  Korean won   1118.20\tab 1118.20\tab    +0.00\par  Baht\tab      37.88\tab   37.82\tab    -0.16\par  Peso\tab      40.93\tab   40.91\tab    -0.04\par  Rupiah\tab  7435.00\tab 7420.00\tab    -0.20\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     105.88\tab  102.21\tab    -3.47\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7123\tab  1.6640\tab    -2.82\par  Taiwan dlr    30.742\tab  31.380\tab    +2.08\par  Korean won   1118.20\tab 1135.00\tab    +1.50\par  Baht\tab      37.88\tab   37.45\tab    -1.14\par  Peso\tab      40.93\tab   40.20\tab    -1.77\par  Rupiah\tab  7435.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -6.19\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Desk (65) 870-3087\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par email:asia.\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 @reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw3f04pc5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
