\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Tokyo leads stocks slide,Taiwan tanks. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Alicia Seow-Suyama \par \uc2 965 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2000\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 13 (Reuters) - Heavy profit-taking in \par \par \uc2  Tokyo technology stocks prompted a sell-off in regional bourses \par \par \uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Nikkei index\tab      fell three percent as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par institutional investors realised gains in high-tech and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Internet stocks ahead of end-March book closings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Retail investors were also keeping away from the sector\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite Nasdaq's record close above the 5,000 level on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Jakarta\tab      succumbed to a late bout of selling after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par initially fending off the regional malaise as buyers chased\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par undervalued stocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PRE-POLL FEARS SPOOK TAIPEI SHARES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taipei stock index\tab      lost a hefty 6.55 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with almost all shares falling by their daily seven-percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limit as nervous investors dumped shares ahead of Saturday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par presidential election.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was hit by fears that already tense ties with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par China could worsen if a pro-independence candidate won the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par election.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Active buying by state and foreign funds should shore up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the stock market but uncertainty remains after the finance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ministry said a T$500 billion ($16.3 billion) stabilisation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund would not be used until after the poll because of an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par opposition boycott.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen buying at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par T$30.77 and this should discourage a sharp drop in the Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINES GETS BOND ROLLING\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippines issued a total $1.6 billion of new bonds in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a two-tranche deal on Friday in line with most market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The first tranche was $600 million of 9.875 percent bonds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due 2010 at a price of 99.95 to yield 9.883 percent, and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par second tranche of $1.0 billion of 10.625 percent bonds due 2025\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at 99.368 to yield 10.698 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Strong demand for the bonds enabled the Philippines to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par increase the size of the sale twice from an initial offer of $1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Robert Voreyer, managing director of high yield debt at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Morgan Stanley Dean Witter in Hong Kong, said most funds chose\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock markets over fixed income markets because they had been\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outperformers over the past few years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I think opportunistically, investors are willing to look\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par at a variety of names, anything from a solid double-B to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par triple-C, as in the case of APP China," he told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par APP China Group Ltd, a subsidiary of Asia Pulp & Paper Co\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par , sold its 10-year senior notes in a private placement\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par through Morgan Stanley Dean Witter last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But I think well-structured deals that are broadly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par distributed will result in fair pricing for both the issuer and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the investor," Voreyer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The APP deal was priced at 86.866 to yield 16.75 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and netted the company about $350 million after $403 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par face value of notes were sold.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WON WANES ON DEFICIT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was weaker, sparked by concerns authorities might\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par step up dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a government official\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ran a trade deficit in early March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Economy official said the country\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par posted a trade deficit of $1.350 billion in the first 10 days\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The figure was slightly larger than the $1.348 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit in the first 10 days of February and far larger than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the $405 million deficit in the same 10 days last March.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The official said the trade deficit was expected to turn to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a surplus by the end of March as exports tend to rise sharply\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par toward the end of the month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea posted a provisional trade surplus of $802\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million for February despite a deficit in the early part of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month. In January, it recorded a trade deficit of $391 million,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its first since October 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0812 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.69\tab  106.30\tab    +0.58\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7044\tab  1.7057\tab    +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr    30.741\tab  30.736\tab    -0.02\par  Korean won   1120.30\tab 1119.30\tab    -0.09\par  Baht\tab      37.81\tab   37.81\tab    +0.00\par  Peso\tab      40.86\tab   40.85\tab    -0.01\par  Rupiah\tab  7396.00\tab 7370.00\tab    -0.35\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7995\tab    +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     105.69\tab  102.21\tab    -3.29\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.7044\tab  1.6640\tab    -2.37\par  Taiwan dlr    30.741\tab  31.380\tab    +2.08\par  Korean won   1120.30\tab 1135.00\tab    +1.31\par  Baht\tab      37.81\tab   37.45\tab    -0.95\par  Peso\tab      40.86\tab   40.20\tab    -1.60\par  Rupiah\tab  7396.00\tab 6975.00\tab    -5.69\par  Ringgit\tab  3.7995\tab  3.7997\tab    +0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ASIAN STOCK MARKETS  0812 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Market\tab  Current\tab Prev Close     Pct Move\par  Tokyo\tab  19189.93     19