\par\par \b \uc2  Korea c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to halt won's rise-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 428 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2000\par 08:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Feb 10 ((Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt the won's steep rise against the dollar, dealers said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank of Korea began to buy dollars after a senior Finance Ministry official said in the afternoon the won's steep appreciation was not desirable for the country's economy. \par \par \uc2  The ministry official also said monetary authorities are closely watching movements of the dollar/won rate. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Korea's direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicates that the 1,120 level will be defended," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state-run banks, such as Korea Development Bank, have been buying dollars since the 1,129 level earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The comments by the ministry official followed the won's surge to 1,119 won to the dollar, influenced by expectations of hefty dollar inflows from foreign buying of local stocks and a drop in the dollar/yen rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The won was trading at 1,120.5 to the dollar at 0701 GMT after rising as high as 1,119.2. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese yen\tab   was quoted at 108.65/70 to the dollar compared with 108.72 late in New York on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Seoul Newsroom +822-727-5645, fax +822-727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Bank of Korea began to buy dollars after a senior Finance Ministry official said in the afternoon the won's steep appreciation was not desirable for the country's economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ministry official also said monetary authorities are closely watching movements of the dollar/won rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Bank of Korea's direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicates that the 1,120 level be defended," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said state-run banks, such as Korea Development Bank, have been buying dollars since the 1,129 level earlier this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The comments by the ministry official followed the won's surge to 1,119 won to the dollar, influenced by expectations of hefty dollar inflows from foreign buying of local stocks and a drop in the dollar/yen rate, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was trading at 1,120.5 to the dollar at 0701 GMT after rising as high as 1,119.2.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Japanese yen\tab   was quoted at 108.65/70 to the dollar compared with 108.72 late in New York on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Seoul Newsroom +822-727-5645, fax +822-727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2a08d68\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
