\par\par \b \uc2  Korea  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to buy dlrs-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2000\par 07:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Jan 20 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea stepped into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in late afternoon trade on Thursday, buying dollars to stem the won's rise as it did earlier in the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the 1,127-1,128 level to shore up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which plunged rapidly in line with a rebound in local stocks, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0632 GMT, the won traded at 1,129.0 to the dollar, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Recovering local stocks helped spur short plays among interbank operators which pushed the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall through the key 1,130 level," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price index saw late gains to end up 7.12 points or 0.76 percent at 945.90. \par \par \uc2  Early in the morning, the BOK stepped in the market and soaked up dollars when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as 1,131.7. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the rise in local stocks would likely limit strong dollar buying by players for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  ((Seoul Newsroom +822-727-5647, fax +822-727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw1k03fo1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
