\par\par \b \uc2  Korea 3-yr yields seen falling from mid-2000 - BOK. \b0\par\par\uc2 429 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2000\par 02:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Jan 19 (Reuters) - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Wednesday he expected the three-year corporate bond yield to begin falling from the middle of the year as the market stabilises. \par \par \uc2  "Generally speaking, although there are some destabilising factors seen for the early part of the year, I expect market interest rates to begin stabilising from the middle of the year," Bank of Korea Governor Chon Chol-hwan said. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a breakfast session for corporate executives hosted by the Korea Chamber of Commerce and Industry, Chon said the current gap between the overnight call rate and the corporate bond yield was too large. \par \par \uc2  "The current gap represents two to three (percentage points of) risk premiums and inflation expectations," Chon said. "I think the gap can be narrowed by about two (percentage points) once the market gains stability." \par \par \uc2  The corporate bond yield closed Tuesday's session at 10.42 percent while the overnight interbank call rate, the short-term benchmark, was up five basis points at 4.65 percent. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market policy, Chon said: "It is not desirable for the exchange rate to change rapidly and the government will take various measures, including smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Under terms for the 1997 bailout package arranged by the International Monetary Fund, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged not to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but was given the right to conduct "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  Summarising recent economic trends, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said the average unemployment rate for the last quarter of calendar 1999 was estimated to have risen to 5.0 percent from 4.4 percent for the previous quarter. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  report distributed at the session showed the number of unemployed stood at an estimated 1.09 million in the October-December period, up from 971,000 in the third quarter. \par \par \uc2  The unemployment average for 1999 is estimated at 6.4 percent with 1.37 million unemployed, compared with 6.8 percent and 1.46 million for 1998. \par \par \uc2  Chon reaffirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forecasts for 2000, including 3.1 percent growth in the consumer price index, the main inflation indicator, up from 0.8 percent for 1999. \par \par \uc2  This year's gross domestic product is forecast to grow by 7.2 percent on year, following growth of a projected 10.2 percent for last year, he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Seoul Newsroom 82-2-727-5646, fax 82-2-727-5666, \par \par \uc2  seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw1j03ftj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
