\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - S.Korea's economic czars target bond yields. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoo Choon-sik \par \uc2 616 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2000\par 07:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Jan 19 (Reuters) - South Korea's top economic planners on Wednesday said long-term interest rates were too high and that cheaper funds were needed to ensure stable economic growth. \par \par \uc2  The finance minister and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said the three-year corporate bond yield - the benchmark long-term interest rate - was unappropriately high. \par \par \uc2  The comments buoyed the domestic bond market and fuelled speculation that authorities would soon announce steps to increase demand for bonds and drive down yields. \par \par \uc2  "Generally speaking, although there are some destabilising factors seen for the early part of the year, I expect market interest rates to begin stabilising from the middle of the year," Bank of Korea governor Chon Chol-hwan said. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a business breakfast hosted by the Korea Chamber of Commerce and Industry, Chon said the gap between the overnight call rate and the corporate bond yield was too large. \par \par \uc2  "The current gap represents two to three (percentage points of) risk premiums and inflation expectations," Chon said. \par \par \uc2  "I think the gap can be narrowed by about two (percentage points) once the market gains stability." \par \par \uc2  The corporate bond yield fell one basis point to 10.41 percent by midday while the overnight interbank call rate, the short-term benchmark, was up six basis points at 4.71 percent. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai, who took the post last week, said separately on Wednesday that local companies would be unable to withstand long-term interest rates of over 10 percent and that the rates must be stabilised below 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  "I think maintaining long-term interest rates below 10 percent is a key policy in aiming to stabilise the economy," said Lee, who had led the country's financial and corporate restructuring over the past two years as head of the financial regulator. \par \par \uc2  DUSTING OFF THE WELCOME MAT \par \par \uc2  Bond traders said there was speculation the government might soon implement a plan to exempt foreign investors from taxes on capital gains and interest earned on domestic government bonds. \par \par \uc2  "Local investors such as investment trusts and banks do not have the (additional) purchasing power to push down the bond yields," said one senior trader at Hyundai Securities. \par \par \uc2  "This has led some in the market to speculate that the government will try to lure a more active participation from offshore-based investors by giving them benefits such as tax exemptions," he added. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministry officials were not available for comment. \par \par \uc2  South Korea lifted most regulations on foreign investment in the domestic bond market in late 1997 in dire efforts to bring in foreign funds and ease the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  shortage. \par \par \uc2  But foreign investment has been lukewarm on Korean bonds, partly because of complicated trading and tax practices and because most Korean issues are rated below investment grade. \par \par \uc2  Asked for a view on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chon read a prepared note summarising the finance ministry's stand. \par \par \uc2  "It is not desirable for the exchange rate to change rapidly and the government will take various measures, including smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Chon said. \par \par \uc2  Under the terms of a 1997 bailout package arranged by the International Monetary Fund, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged not to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but was given the right to conduct "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to stabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  South Korea fears the won's rapid appreciation could hurt exports, which have yet to fully recover their momentum, by depriving exporters of price advantages. \par \par \uc2  The won ended Wednesday's morning session at the previous day's closing rate of 1,127.0 per dollar after ranging from 1,126.0 to 1,132.0. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010820dw1j03deg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
