\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Nikkei rallies as Wall St steadies. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Tamora Vidaillet \par \uc2 1,053 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2000\par 10:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Jan 17 (Reuters) - Reassurance over the tame \par \par \uc2  nature of U.S. inflation lifted many Asian markets on Monday, \par \par \uc2  though Hong Kong and the Philippines were weighed down by \par \par \uc2  lingering interest rate fears. \par \par \uc2      Most markets drew their strength from a record closing high \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the Dow Jones industrial index\tab     and fresh gains in the\par technology-laden Nasdaq composite index\tab      on Friday, after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par key U.S. inflation data for December came in lower than\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     CPI rose 0.2 percent, compared to expectations for an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par average 0.3 percent increase according to a recent Reuters poll.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That fuelled buying in Japan's Nikkei 225\tab     , pushing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it to its highest close in two and a half years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Laggard Malaysian stocks, meanwhile, stole the limelight\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with gains of more than four percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bright mood in stocks rubbed off onto most regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , forcing the monetary authorities in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain vigilant against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharp upward pressure.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore stocks bucked the regional up-trend, shedding\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more than two percent as fund managers banked profits and some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par re-weighted their portfolios, shifting money into markets like\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Malaysia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FUND NEWS BOLSTERS TAIEX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Plans to launch a T$500 billion (US$16.2 billion) stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilisation fund to absorb potential shocks to Taiwan shares\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and a further loosening of restrictions for foreign investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lifted the TAIEX to a 28-month closing high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The index ended 2.1 percent higher, with local brokers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par anticipating a rise to 9,500 or 10,000 sometime soon despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely bouts of profit-taking along the way.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Buying was focused more on traditional industrial sectors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par than on recently high-flying technology counters, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan's parliament approved a cabinet proposal to set up a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stabilisation fund at the weekend, aimed at keeping the stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market on an even keel in case relations with China\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deteriorated.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although this could avert tremors like those last year when\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par souring relations caused Taiwan stocks to dive 14 percent, some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par analysts were sceptical of the political motives behind the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As an institutional investor, I would be sceptical as to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether this is positive...I would obviously question the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par motives for the government to invest in their own stock market,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Robert Penaloza, investment manager at Aberdeen Asset\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Management, told Reuters Television.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The government should perhaps stick to liberalisation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par measures that they're looking to implement...like allowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreigners to list their shares into the market or even enabling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par them to buy more shares in state-owned banks," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The island's financial regulator also moved to ease listing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rules for foreign firms to improve the market's international\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profile. Foreign firms can now list a minimum 20 million shares\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par locally instead of 30 million and they only need to show annual\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit growth of six percent instead of eight percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par previously.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREA POLICY SEEN UNCHANGED\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , led by newly appointed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par minister Lee Hun-jai, announced its economic targets for 2000\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and indicated no change in economic policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It said it expected the economy to expand around six\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent in 2000 after growing an estimated 10 percent in 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     It also said it would aim to stabilise long-term interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates below 10 percent this year and focus on containing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation under three percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The country's current account surplus was expected to total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $12 billion in 2000, compared with an estimated $26 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surplus for 1999, it said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won firmed to its highest level since late 1997 early\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the day as foreign funds extended their recent stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shopping spree but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took it off its intraday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bank's renewed efforts to temper the speed of its rise\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were somewhat mixed, with the won ending the day at 1,121 -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its strongest finish versus the dollar since November 1997.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ways were also set to continue in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par domestic bond market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The top manager of the country's bond market stabilisation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund, Paik Kyung-Ho, said the fund would continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market until February 8, when investors in Daewoo Group\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  bond funds can redeem up to 95 percent of their money\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared to 80 percent now.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0825 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     105.15\tab  105.61\tab    +0.44\par  Sing dlr\tab 1.6737\tab  1.6730\tab    -0.04\par  Taiwan dlr     30.80\tab   30.82\tab    +0.06\par  Korean won   1120.30\