\par\par \b \uc2  Korea won closes lower, reined in by  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1999\par 10:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, Dec 9 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's won\tab     -2 weakened against the dollar on Thursday, sent back into the 1,130s by direct dollar buying by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and government verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well as short dollar covering by banks, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Trade was light as most players were concerned over direct dollar sales by the Bank of Korea, they said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The won ended the day at 1,130.1 compared with Wednesday's close of 1,126.0. \par \par \uc2  It opened at 1,127.0 and ranged between 1,125.0 and 1,135.0. \par \par \uc2  "Trades were mostly inactive for the day as strong early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept players out of the market with no noticeable orders spotted," said a dealer at a domestic bank. \par \par \uc2  Before the opening bell, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy made comments they would act on the won's rise to prevent export competitiveness from deteriorating. \par \par \uc2  With the market shrugging off those remarks, the Bank of Korea came into the market and bought dollars aimed at showing the authorities' strong intention to stem the won's rise, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "While the won's rise was checked for the day, the market is still dollar-heavy as a number of domestic firms are lined up for dollar sales," said another dealer at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  He said the authorities do not have much room to step into the market directly not only because of inflationary risks but also a lack of the local unit. \par \par \uc2  "They are saying they are going to issue \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds to secure the won but for now that looks hazy as the government is still preoccupied with preventing interest rates from getting out of hand," he said. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon, the finance ministry pointed out that the state-run Korea Asset Management Corp (KAMCO) is ready to take over foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated bad loans from banks. \par \par \uc2  It said to do so, KAMCO could secure dollars from the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Speculative players in the offshore market were also on the sidelines, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the won/dollar pair is seen moving in a similar range, they said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In late trade, the won/yen rate stood at 10.94/96 compared to 10.94/95 late Wednesday, while the Japanese unit was at 103.05/08\tab   versus the dollar, compared to 102.78/81 late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The six-month non-deliverable forward won stood at 1,131/33 as of 0700 GMT versus 1,128/30 late Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The one-year non-deliverable forward won was quoted at 1,138/40 versus 1,136/38. ((Kim Kyoung-Wha, Seoul Newsroom +822-727-5647, fax +822-727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc908opf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
