\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed as yen slips in cautious trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 1999\par 04:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0155 GMT - Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed in early \par \par \uc2  trade, with the dollar higher against the yen amid \par \par \uc2  short-covering ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2      Traders in Tokyo said the yen still had a firm bias as \par \par \uc2  investors remained keen to buy the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But the market was cautious about pushing it up \par \par \uc2  aggressively ahead of a weekend meeting of deputy finance \par \par \uc2  ministers and central bankers of the 14 Manila Framework member \par \par \uc2  countries in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Jitters over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Japan to \par \par \uc2  tame the yen swirled around the market overnight but the fears \par \par \uc2  were spurred by a stream of vague rumours. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah was holding steady despite news Indonesia's \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had found evidence of crimes in the Bank Bali \par \par \uc2  scandal . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Subarjo Joyosumarto told \par \par \uc2  reporters after a meeting with police officials on Thursday \par \par \uc2  that a controversial interbank loan had not been recorded in \par \par \uc2  the bank's financial reports. \par \par \uc2      The findings have been passed to the police for \par \par \uc2  investigation. \par \par \uc2      Fresh violence between supporters and opponents of \par \par \uc2  independence in East Timor is another factor that could \par \par \uc2  pressure the rupiah. \par \par \uc2      At least three people were killed in violent clashes on \par \par \uc2  Thursday, casting a shadow over the troubled territory's final \par \par \uc2  day of campaigning for a U.N.-organised referendum on \par \par \uc2  independence, due on Monday. \par \par \uc2  *** The peso was little changed in pre-weekend trade. \par \par \uc2  All eyes are on a weekly meeting of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2  Monetary Board amid expectations of a hike in bank reserve \par \par \uc2  requirements. \par \par \uc2  The peso is teetering at nine-month lows due to the \par \par \uc2  narrower spreads between domestic and U.S. interest rates, \par \par \uc2  exacerbated by the Federal Reserve rate hike on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said on Thursday \par \par \uc2  he might have to raise bank reserve requirements if domestic \par \par \uc2  Treasury bill yields fail to rise at Monday's auction. \par \par \uc2  Philippine production indexes showed mixed results in June, \par \par \uc2  with value up 2.3 percent on a year earlier and volume down 1.1 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2  The government is due to release second quarter GDP data \par \par \uc2  around 0230 GMT. Socio-economic Planning Secretary Felipe \par \par \uc2  Medalla said on Thursday the economy may have grown 3.0 percent \par \par \uc2  on the year in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2      *** Hong Kong is also due to report second quarter GDP \par \par \uc2  numbers at around 0800 GMT. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters poll of 11 economists produced an average \par \par \uc2  forecast for a 1.2 percent contraction in the second quarter \par \par \uc2  from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2      The government on Thursday reported a significant \par \par \uc2  turnaround in trade performance, with total exports in July \par \par \uc2  rising 3.0 percent year-on-year and July imports up 3.7 \par \par \uc2  percent. \par \par \uc2  They were the first year-on-year rises in both categories \par \par \uc2  since early 1998. Chief government economist K.Y. Tang said \par \par \uc2  they supported his forecast that second quarter GDP would be \par \par \uc2  flat from a year ago, or at least contract at a slower rate \par \par \uc2  than in the year to the first quarter. \par \par \uc2      July month-on-month increases in exports and imports came \par \par \uc2  in at 10.9 percent and 10.4 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2      *** \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won headed lower as fears of government \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to pervade the market. \par \par \uc2      A meeting between Daewoo and foreign creditors, originally \par \par \uc2  set for Friday, has been delayed. A Daewoo spokesman told \par \par \uc2  Reuters that both sides needed more time to include Thursday's \par \par \uc2  new debt workout programme in their negotiation plans. \par \par \uc2      The spokesman thought it unlikely that the meeting would \par \par \uc2  take place anytime this week. \par \par \uc2      Daewoo's creditors decided on Thursday to put the embattled \par \par \uc2  conglomerate's 12 core companies under a workout programme, \par \par \uc2  freezing debt payments temporarily while creditors take over \par \par \uc2  managerial control and discuss debt rescheduling. \par \par \uc2  The government will support the process through a series \par \par \uc2  of \par \par \uc2  measures, which include guaranteeing the discounting of \par \par \uc2  commercial paper issued by Daewoo firms. \par \par \uc2  *** Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said on \par \par \uc2  Thursday that the ringgit would remain pegged at 3.80 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar, but added that he did not know if the peg would \par \par \uc2  continue for another year. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said the present system of capital \par \par \uc2  gains taxes of foreign portfolio investments would remain. \par \par \uc2      The first anniversary of capital controls imposed in \par \par \uc2  Malaysia to protect the economy from speculators falls on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day FRI 27 0122GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest bid....Prev Close.....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.......7630.00......7650.00.........0.26% \par \par \uc2   Baht.........38.35........38.31..........-0.10% \par \par \uc2   Peso.........39.76........39.73..........-0.08% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6913.......1.6903.........-0.06% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.810.......31.820..........0.03% \par \par \uc2   Korean won...1191.80......1190.00........-0.15% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....111.72...... 110.96.........-0.68% \par \par \uc2   Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest........July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah.......7630.00......2432.00.......-68.13% \par \par \uc2   Baht.........38.39........25.90.........-32.53% \par \par \uc2   Peso.........39.76........26.50.........-33.35% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.6913.......1.4300........-15.45% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...31.8100......27.7500.......-12.76% \par \par \uc2   Korean won...1191.80......842.00........-29.35% \par \par \uc2   Japan yen....111.72.......114.40..........2.40% \par \par \uc2      ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010