\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Regionals end firmer, yen gains ground. \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1999\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0930 GMT - The Asian regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were firmer in \par \par \uc2  late business with the yen getting to its highest level since \par \par \uc2  mid-February. \par \par \uc2  The markets are watchful ahead of the second half of U.S. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's Humphrey-Hawkins \par \par \uc2  testimony before the Senate Banking Committee. \par \par \uc2  The Fed has said that Greenspan's speech, scheduled for \par \par \uc2  1400 GMT, would mostly be a rehash of the previous week's \par \par \uc2  comments. Market analysts saw this as an attempt to calm \par \par \uc2  financial markets. \par \par \uc2  *** The rupiah gained as the market remains uncertain about \par \par \uc2  the political backdrop. \par \par \uc2  But the authorities are still trying to talk it up with \par \par \uc2  top economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita saying 6,000 would be a \par \par \uc2  good level. \par \par \uc2  "At the present moment, a value of around 6,500 is \par \par \uc2  comfortable," he said. "There is room for improvement. Around \par \par \uc2  6,000 would be a good figure for us." \par \par \uc2  But he also said there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get the \par \par \uc2  rupiah to 6,000. \par \par \uc2  Ginandjar is in Paris meeting with international donors. \par \par \uc2  Bank Indonesia governor Syahril Sabirin said the interest \par \par \uc2  rate on one-month \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates will fall less than \par \par \uc2  one percentage point at the weekly auction scheduled for later. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Indonesia's net foreign reserves rose to $16.15 \par \par \uc2  billion on July 23 from $16.11 billion on July 15. \par \par \uc2  *** \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won was firmer despite ongoing verbal \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the government and dollar purchases by \par \par \uc2  state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said state-run banks mopped up nearly $400 million \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday and it seemed the government was resolved to keep \par \par \uc2  dollar/won above 1,200. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kang Bong-kyun said creditors will \par \par \uc2  eventually liquidate $8.3 billion in collateral put up by \par \par \uc2  Daewoo Group in return for four trillion won in emergency \par \par \uc2  loans. \par \par \uc2  Creditors are expected to whittle down the chaebol's 22 \par \par \uc2  affiliates to just two firms and sell most of the rest. \par \par \uc2  This followed the government's move on Tuesday to leave the \par \par \uc2  fate of the embattled conglomerate squarely in its creditors' \par \par \uc2  hands. \par \par \uc2  In other news, June's current account surplus was reported \par \par \uc2  at $2.46 billion, down from $3.39 billion a year ago but up \par \par \uc2  from $1.99 billion in May 1999. \par \par \uc2  Exports in June rose 10.6 percent year-on-year to $12.78 \par \par \uc2  billion, and imports spiked 31.2 percent to $9.85 billion. \par \par \uc2  From January to June 1999, exports rose 0.7 percent to \par \par \uc2  $67.58 billion year-on-year, and imports rose 14.4 percent to \par \par \uc2  $52.50 billion. \par \par \uc2  *** The Singapore dollar firmed, but gains were limited \par \par \uc2  amid rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday when the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to six-month highs. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Lee Hsien Loong told Reuters Television \par \par \uc2  that the country's growth forecast for the year will be \par \par \uc2  upgraded following better-than-expected performance in the \par \par \uc2  second quarter. \par \par \uc2  The revised forecast will be announced on August 9, \par \par \uc2  Singapore's National Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  Lee also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "very comfortable" with \par \par \uc2  the level of the Sing dollar on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Change on the day WED 28 0927GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2  Ringgit......3.7999.......3.8000.........0.00% \par \par \uc2  Rupiah......6860.00......6960.00.........1.46% \par \par \uc2  Baht..........37.02........37.27.........0.68% \par \par \uc2  Peso..........38.22........38.20........-0.05% \par \par \uc2  Sing dlr.....1.6790.......1.6900.........0.66% \par \par \uc2  Taiwan dlr...32.205.......32.230.........0.08% \par \par \uc2  Korean won..1198.00......1203.00.........0.42% \par \par \uc2  Japan yen....115.82.......116.38.........0.48% \par \par \uc2  Change since start of Asia crisis \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .....Latest......July '97......Pct Move \par \par \uc2  Ringgit......3.7999.......2.5200........-33.68% \par \par \uc2  Rupiah......6860.00......2432.00........-64.55% \par \par \uc2  Baht..........37.24........25.90........-30.45% \par \par \uc2  Peso..........38.22........26.50........-30.66% \par \par \uc2  Sing dlr.....1.6790.......1.4300........-14.83% \par \par \uc2  Taiwan dlr..32.2050......27.7500........-13.83% \par \par \uc2  Korean won..1198.00.......842.00........-29.72% \par \par \uc2  Japan yen....115.82.......114.40.........-1.23% \par \par \uc2  ((Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840;fax (65) 870-3787; email: \par \par \uc2  asi