\par\par \b \uc2  Korea won ends little lower, exporters limit loss. \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1999\par 10:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, June 30 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\tab   closed slightly weaker against the dollar on Wednesday mainly due to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but export deals limited the won's further decline.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Bank of Korea bought about $100 million to $150 million in early trade. But the bank declined to confirm the action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The won closed at 1,157.6, compared with Tuesday's close of 1,157.0. It opened at 1,157.5 and ranged between 1,156.0 and 1,162.5. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases lifted the dollar trading level above 1,160 won, but export deals were lined up at that level," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sales by offshore players also pulled the dollar lower, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  A foreign bank dealer said local banks placed strong bids to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  "It shows that the local banks had a psychological pressure to follow the government's move to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he said. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, assistant governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  urged local bank directors that the banks set aside \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  loan-loss provisions in their positions, a move which would soak up at least $2 billion from the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market largely ignored the inflation data, as the market concentrated on other factors like exporter deals and government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry said on Wednesday the inflation rate, gauged by the consumer price index (CPI), was an average of 0.6 percent for the six months of this year, the lowest six-month figure since 1965 when South Korea began to keep records on inflation. \par \par \uc2  The six-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) won was quoted at 1,160/63 won, while the one-year stood at 1,165/67. \par \par \uc2  ((Kim Se-yoon, Seoul Newsroom +82 2 727 5650, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6u05aea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
