\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won opens almost flat, eyes on govt moves. \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 03:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, June 25 (Reuters) - The South Korean won\tab   opened barely changed against the dollar on Friday, and traders said they would continue to watch for verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by government officals or dollar purchases by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won opened at 1,158.0, compared with Thursday's close of 1,157.9.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Friday's mid-rate was pegged at 1,160.3. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar would remain under downward pressure during the day, pressured by month-end exporter deals. \par \par \uc2  "Players would be cautious in trading because of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the government, but the dollar won't be able to escape from pressure to fall," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Another dealer said: "The government will feel burdened to absorb dollars today because the market is heavy with the greenback." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the commerce minister's comment on the exchange rate had little impact on the market as verbal comments by government officials had lost their market-moving power. \par \par \uc2  "The government would do its best so that the won/dollar rate does not hurt exports," said minister Chung Duck-koo at a breakfast meeting. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose on Thursday on news that Fitch IBCA upgraded Korea's sovereign ratings and on comments by IMF's Hubert Neiss. \par \par \uc2  Neiss said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was not aimed at weakening the won, but at smoothing the won's movement. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar would move between 1,155 and 1,160. \par \par \uc2  The six-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) won was quoted at 1,158/61 won, while the one-year stood at 1,160/63. \par \par \uc2  ((Kim Se-yoon, Seoul Newsroom +82 2 727 5650, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6p05vp0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
