\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS-Stocks stirred, not shaken by Wall St. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Phil Smith \par \uc2 945 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 1999\par 11:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 25 (Reuters) - An overnight drop on Wall \par \par \uc2  Street took the shine off Asian stocks on Friday, though South \par \par \uc2  Korean and Thai markets were comforted by credit-rating \par \par \uc2  upgrades. \par \par \uc2      THAILAND BACK AT INVESTMENT GRADE \par \par \uc2      Fitch IBCA put Thailand back on investment grade, citing a \par \par \uc2  marked improvement in external debt and the liquidity \par \par \uc2  situation. \par \par \uc2      It raised Thailand's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to \par \par \uc2  BBB minus from BB plus and its short-term rating to F3 from B. \par \par \uc2      The news was well received by Thai stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  markets, especially after Moody's Investors Services said this \par \par \uc2  week that Thai banks remained heavily insolvent. \par \par \uc2      But the government said the Moody's report was outdated and \par \par \uc2  failed to take into account Thailand's bigger banks, which have \par \par \uc2  been recapitalised. \par \par \uc2      Thailand's annual budget, now before parliament, forecasts \par \par \uc2  one percent growth this year and three percent for 2000, with \par \par \uc2  inflation seen at just 0.5 percent this year and three percent \par \par \uc2  next. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Finance Minister Pisit Leeatham said Thailand was \par \par \uc2  happy with the level of the baht, which strengthened sharply \par \par \uc2  this week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  curb its rise. \par \par \uc2  But in a sign that competitiveness was a source of concern, \par \par \uc2  Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panitchpakdi said the baht would \par \par \uc2  be too strong for exports if it reached 35 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  KOSPI HOLDS UP, WON HEADS FOR 1,150 \par \par \uc2  Seoul stocks managed a slightly firmer finish despite some \par \par \uc2  profit-taking after Wall Street's fall. \par \par \uc2      But traders said sentiment was lifted by Fitch IBCA's move \par \par \uc2  to upgrade South Korea's sovereign ratings on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      Fitch raised the long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating to BBB \par \par \uc2  from BBB-, citing the strong reassertion of South Korea's \par \par \uc2  traditional economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2      The won gained from exporter dollar sales, but its rise was \par \par \uc2  held in check by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \par \par \uc2  commerce ministry said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  would try to keep won-dollar \par \par \uc2  movements from hurting exports. But analysts said the won \par \par \uc2  remained on a longer-term uptrend and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar \par \par \uc2  buying was increasingly being viewed as an effort to smooth, \par \par \uc2  rather than stop its rise. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is intent on keeping the won quite stable in \par \par \uc2  the short term," said Thio Chin Loo, strategist at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  "But longer term, there should be a greater appetite from \par \par \uc2  the authorities to allow the won to strengthen with signs of \par \par \uc2  economic growth and with some inflationary pressures," she told \par \par \uc2  Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN SHARES SUCCUMB TO RATE FEARS \par \par \uc2  Taiwan stocks lost a hefty 3.76 percent on huge net selling \par \par \uc2  by local mutual funds and worries over a possible tightening of \par \par \uc2  monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      The market appears jittery over a possible rate rise and \par \par \uc2  traders reckon support at 8,200 points could be tested soon. \par \par \uc2      There's a gap that has yet to be filled on the daily chart \par \par \uc2  and it will be worth watching carefully for another gap forming \par \par \uc2  on the way down. This would form an island reversal top which \par \par \uc2  is a classic trend reversal pattern. \par \par \uc2      Korea's KOSPI did just this in January and didn't stop \par \par \uc2  falling until late February. \par \par \uc2      KL SHARES RISE, ECONOMIC OUTLOOK IMPROVES \par \par \uc2      Kuala Lumpur stocks were slightly higher, but struggling to \par \par \uc2  make serious headway above 800 points despite an improving \par \par \uc2  economic outlook. \par \par \uc2      Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said the economy was \par \par \uc2  growing well but did not revise the official 1999 GDP forecast \par \par \uc2  of one percent. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said up to three percent growth is \par \par \uc2  possible but the market is more in tune with Mahathir, with the \par \par \uc2  latest Reuters poll seeing 1.3 percent growth this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par \par \uc2   Change on the day FRI 25 0900GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move \par \par \uc2   Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000.........0.01% \par \par \uc2   Rupiah......6910.00......6735.00........-2.53% \par \par \uc2   Baht..........36.65........36.68.........0.08% \par \par \uc2   Peso..........37.88........37.86........-0.05% \par \par \uc2   Sing dlr.....1.7028.......1.7000........-0.16% \par \par \uc2   Taiwan dlr...32.310.......32.350.........0.12% \par 