\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korean won weaker by noon, govt/c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1999\par 05:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 23 (Reuters) - Government verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea pushed the South Korean won   lower versus the dollar by midday on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said dollar unloading from exporter deals continued to pressure the dollar versus the won. \par \par \uc2  The won stood at 1,163.5 by midday, compared with Tuesday's close of 1,159.4. It opened at 1,160.0 and ranged between 1,158.5 and 1,167.0. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea absorbed about $300 million from the opening bell in an attempt to stop the won from rising. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases did lift the dollar's value, but they won't be able to outweigh the pressure (on dollar) from exporter deals," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said exporter deals were lined up at 1,165.0 won and dollars continued to flow into the market. \par \par \uc2  They said the market has little affected by verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Market players are not afraid of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  any more," said a foreign bank dealer. "The dollar will not rise unless there is another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry officials said the government was closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and that it would take effective measures to slow the won's rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Kang Bong-kyun said the government would try to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The government won't directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to meet a targeted rate but it will try to fulfill its role (to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)," Kang said. \par \par \uc2  A stronger won makes it difficult for the country's exporters to compete in international markets, especially against Japanese goods. The two countries compete head ot head on cars, ships and electronics. \par \par \uc2  Traders forecast the dollar would move between 1,160 and 1,165 won in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  They would keep their eyes on further \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  or dollar purchases by state-run banks. \par \par \uc2  The six-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) won was quoted at 1,166/68 won, while the one-year stood at 1,169/71. \par \par \uc2  ((Kim Se-yoon, Seoul Newsroom +82 2 727 5650, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6n05z0d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
