\par\par \b \uc2  POLL-S.Korea won seen rising to 1,148 by end-1999. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Jean Yoon \par \uc2 802 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SEOUL, June 14 (Reuters) - The South Korean won is set to \par \par \uc2  gain ground in the coming months, lifted by the country's \par \par \uc2  current account surplus and a heavy inflow of foreign direct \par \par \uc2  and portfolio investments, a Reuters poll showed. \par \par \uc2      But the government, fearful its exporters may lose leverage \par \par \uc2  because of the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would try to control the pace \par \par \uc2  of the won's appreciation. \par \par \uc2      A Reuters poll of 11 interbank dealers and economists \par \par \uc2  showed an average forecast of 1,156 won per dollar at the end \par \par \uc2  of September and 1,148 at the end of this year. \par \par \uc2      The won, which is not fully convertible, stood at 1,171.5 \par \par \uc2  won per dollar by Monday midday. It is up nearly three percent \par \par \uc2  so far this year. \par \par \uc2      "How the government induces dollar demand is the key to \par \par \uc2  slowing the pace of the dollar's fall," said Kim Hee-byung, a \par \par \uc2  fixed income analyst at Samsung Securities. \par \par \uc2      "The government realises it can't reverse the trend, but it \par \par \uc2  will try to manipulate the market to manage the pace." \par \par \uc2      Kim forecast the won would rise to 1,150 by the end of \par \par \uc2  September. \par \par \uc2      The financial crisis that crippled Korea in late 1997 was \par \par \uc2  triggered by a dire shortage of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that \par \par \uc2  situation has since turned around. \par \par \uc2      South Korea recorded a current account surplus of $8.80 \par \par \uc2  billion in the January-April period, compared with a $14.42 \par \par \uc2  billion surplus a year earlier. Foreign direct investment plans \par \par \uc2  in the first five months totalled $3.48 billion, up 93.3 \par \par \uc2  percent from $1.80 billion in the same period last year. \par \par \uc2  Fears of a renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis have waned and \par \par \uc2  South Korea is now worried about the won's climb against the \par \par \uc2  dollar. \par \par \uc2  A finance ministry official said on Monday that the \par \par \uc2  ministry was closely watching the won/dollar exchange rate, and \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on three days last week, \par \par \uc2  buying a combined $250 million to $260 million. \par \par \uc2  But analysts doubted the won's trend would be reversed. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be limited to containing the pace, not \par \par \uc2  the course," said a dealer at a European bank, who saw the \par \par \uc2  local unit at 1,050 by the year-end. \par \par \uc2      "A steady inflow of foreign funds, an increase in exports \par \par \uc2  and corporate asset sales would pull the dollar down," he said. \par \par \uc2      Korea, a major exporter, worries the rising won will hurt \par \par \uc2  its competitiveness and smother its nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2      A stronger won makes it harder for Korean exporters to \par \par \uc2  compete in global markets, especially against Japanese goods \par \par \uc2  such as cars, ships and electronics. \par \par \uc2      "The government will try hard to protect the country's \par \par \uc2  exports, but it cannot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the way it did before the \par \par \uc2  crisis because of the agreement with the International Monetary \par \par \uc2  Fund," said Lee Chang-seon, an economist at LG Economic \par \par \uc2  Research Institute. \par \par \uc2  The IMF arranged a $58.35 billion rescue package in \par \par \uc2  December 1997 for South Korea, and most of the country's key \par \par \uc2  economic policy decisions are made in consultation with the \par \par \uc2  IMF. \par \par \uc2  The IMF said last week \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced no restraints in \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth day-to-day volatility on the local \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2      But some analysts expected calls for even more government \par \par \uc2  latitude. \par \par \uc2      "The government is likely to try to convince the IMF during \par \par \uc2  its next policy meeting with Korea that it needs to be able to \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly," said Lee, who expects the won to rise to \par \par \uc2  1,150 by the end of 1999. \par \par \uc2      Korea is set to meet with IMF representatives for two weeks \par \par \uc2  starting from June 30 for a quarterly policy review. \par \par \uc2      But not everyone was bullish on the won. \par \par \uc2      Stephen Marvin, head of research at Jardine Fleming \par \par \uc2  Securities, saw the won slipping to 1,250 in the last quarter. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar would rise towards the end of the year as \par \par \uc2  foreign direct and portfolio investments shrink and a decrease \par \par \uc2  in the trade surplus accelerates," Marvin said. \par \par \uc2      TABLE OF FORECASTS FOR THE WON/DOLLAR RATE: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Institution\tab \tab end-Sept\tab    end-1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Kookmin Bank\tab \tab     1,150\tab \tab 1,120 Citibank\par \tab \tab     1,130\tab \tab 1,100 LG Economic Research\par    1,170\tab \tab 1,150 HSBC\tab \tab \tab \tab 1,120\par \tab  1,050 Daewoo Research\tab \tab  1,180\tab \tab 1,150\par Korea Exchange Bank\tab    1,180\tab \tab 1,200 Samsung\par Securities\tab     1,150\tab 1,110-1,150 Bank of America\par \tab  1,150\tab \tab 1,130 Hyundai Research\tab \tab   ~\par \tab      1,150 Korea Development Bank\tab 1,180\par 1,200 Jardine Fleming\tab \tab  1,150\tab \tab 1,250\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Average\tab \tab      1,156\tab \tab 1,148\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ----------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Note - A Reuters poll conducted in April had an average\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forecast dollar/won rate of 1,156.7 won at the end of 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Seoul newsroom, +822 727-5643, Fax +822 727-5666,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06m63\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
