\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won closes weaker on yen's tumble. \b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 10:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 14 (Reuters) - The South Korean won closed weaker on Monday in line with the Japanese yen's tumble after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Japan's early morning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But dollar sales by some corporations managed to cushion the weakness of the won towards the end of the day, brokers said. \par \par \uc2  The won closed at 1,170 per dollar, compared with Friday's 1,167.6 finish. It opened at 1,168.5 and ranged between 1,167 and 1,173. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar rallied against the won early in the morning closely tracking the U.S. unit's strength against yen," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen stood at 120.46/51 per dollar in late Tokyo off Friday's 117.88/98 in late New York and 118.75/85 in late Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan was seen buying dollars in the upper end of the range from 120 to 121 yen per dollar towards the end of the afternoon, Japanese bankers said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ had been detected in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market throughout the day on Monday since initially stepping in around 118.20 yen per dollar early in the morning, they said. \par \par \uc2  In the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers were also cautious about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by state banks in the late afternoon, following last week's pattern. \par \par \uc2  Two state-run banks were seen to have bought about $250 million in the previous three trading days, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean finance ministry reaffirmed its willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying in the early morning it was "keeping a close eye on the won/dollar exchange rate." \par \par \uc2  "It is not advisable for the South Korean won's exchange rate (against the U.S. dollar) to move in a different direction from the yen/dollar movement," a finance ministry official, who did not wish to be identified, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Market sources interpreted the latest verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a cooperative effort between \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan, following an early morning \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank of Japan in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The remarks appear to be targeting some corporations' dollar sales and affirming the strength of last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , local dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea governor Chon Chol-hwan told Reuters in an interview on Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  consulted with the International Monetary Fund before directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "The government consults with the IMF before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market even for 'smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 '," Governor Chon Chol-hwan told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  But his remaks had little impact on the won/dollar rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Reuters poll of 11 interbank dealers and economists showed the the won was likely to gain further ground in the coming months, while the government would try to control the the pace of the won's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  A stronger won hurts South Korean export competitiveness in global markets, especially against Japanese products. \par \par \uc2  The poll showed an average forecast of 1,156 won per dollar at the end of September and 1,148 at the end of this year. \par \par \uc2  The six-month non-deliverable forward (NDF) won was quoted at 1,173.5/75.0 per dollar, while the one-year stood at 1,176/79. \par \par \uc2  ((Koo Hee-jin, Seoul Newsroom +822 727 5648, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06lgs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
