\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea says consults IMF on  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  consults with the International Monetary Fund before directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The government consults with the IMF before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market even for 'smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 '," Bank of Korea Governor Chon Chol-hwan told Reuters in an interview. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in three trading days of last week, buying approximately $250 million to $260 million to prop up the dollar against the won, market sources said. \par \par \uc2  The sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars shortly after the IMF's senior representative in Seoul, John Dodsworth, told Reuters that the IMF was not restraining \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth day-to-day volatility on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "There is an agreement between the government and the IMF concerning market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when it is direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and not indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Chon said. \par \par \uc2  But he added that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government's basic policy is to let the exchange rate be determined freely by market forces to reflect the country's fundamentals such as the current account and movements of other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The country has adopted the free-floating exchange rate regime and the exchange rate will be determined by market forces," Chon said. \par \par \uc2  But he said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities would indirectly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever "there is a market supply and demand disparity". \par \par \uc2  The authorities would properly implement indirect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures such as rescheduling of external debt replayments when such disparity occur, he said. \par \par \uc2  Chon said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also calling in some $20 billion it had extended to domestic banks last year to ease a liquidity crisis, as a way of controlling the supply of dollars on the market. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won finished at 1,170 per dollar, compared to Friday's close of 1,167.6. \par \par \uc2  ((Seoul newsroom, +82 2 727 5642, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06lau\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
