\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of Korea  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars-dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1999\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to buy dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market shortly before the close of trade on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm the move. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to buy about $100 million," said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came a little after the International Monetary Fund reaffirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced no restraints in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth day-to-day volatility on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Since the beginning of the IMF-supported programme, there has never been any intention to constrain the authorities in their day-to-day smoothing out of volatility of the exchange rate," the IMF's chief representative in Korea John Dodsworth told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on each of the past two days, buying more than $100 million on Thursday and $50 million to $60 million on Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Korea is concerned the won's appreciation will hurt its export competitiveness and its nascent economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A stronger won makes it difficult for the country's exporters to compete in international markets, especially against Japanese goods. The two countries compete head to head on cars, ships and electronics. \par \par \uc2  ((Seoul newsroom, +822 727-5643, Fax +822 727-5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6b06leg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
