\par\par \b \uc2  IMF-Korea can  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to smooth  \highlight22\uc2 forex operations \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1999\par 09:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 11 (Reuters) - The International Monetary Fund on Friday reaffirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced no restraints in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth day-to-day volatility on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "Since the beginning of the IMF-supported programme, there has never been any intention to constrain the authorities in their day-to-day smoothing out of volatility of the exchange rate," the IMF's chief representative in Korea John Dodsworth told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in Korea is still developing and it is important that the authorities retain such freedom to effectively implement smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Dodsworth said. \par \par \uc2  The latest quarterly memorandum on economic policies agreed between the IMF and the Korean government calls for a flexible exchange rate policy. \par \par \uc2  "Exchange rate policy will remain flexible and Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be limited to smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  consistent with achieving the reserve target," said the policy review. \par \par \uc2  Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea had stepped into the market on Wednesday and Thursday and bought an estimated $150 million to $160 million over the two days. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's finance ministry said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been repeatedly buying dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to contain the won's rise. \par \par \uc2  "The purpose is to maintain the supply and demand, to maintain a balanced market," ministry spokeswoman Kang Yeoun-sun told Reuters Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  "Over a mid-term to long-term, we'd like to maintain a healthy amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and also maintain a positive current account balance for 1999," Kang said. \par \par \uc2  "The other thing is making sure there's fairness and prudential regulation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." \par \par \uc2  Dodsworth underlined that market forces have to be respected in determining the underlying exchange rate trends. \par \par \uc2  "Of course, in determining the underlying trend of the exchange rate, market forces have to be respected and this is the only way to develop a more mature \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the IMF chief representative said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6b06le9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
