\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea acknowledges  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 465 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1999\par 07:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, June 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry said on Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been repeatedly buying dollars in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to contain the won's rise. \par \par \uc2  "The purpose is to maintain the supply and demand, to maintain a balanced market," ministry spokeswoman Kang Yeoun-sun told Reuters Television in an interview. \par \par \uc2  She was responding to a question about why the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this week. \par \par \uc2  "Over a mid-term to long-term, we'd like to maintain a healthy amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and also maintain a positive current account balance for 1999," Kang said. \par \par \uc2  "The other thing is making sure there's fairness and prudential regulation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market." \par \par \uc2  Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea had stepped into the market on Wednesday and Thursday and bought an estimated $150 million to $160 million over the two days. \par \par \uc2  This is the first time a government official has confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In the past government officials declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  The government has frequently expressed concerns that the steep appreciation of the won versus the dollar could seriously hamper the country's exports because a stronger won would make South Korean exports more expensive. \par \par \uc2  Kang said the government was not targetting the dollar/won rate at a specific level but was aiming to keep the rate within a stable range. \par \par \uc2  "I'd like to say that the finance ministry is not so much concerned about the recent movements of the won/dollar rate, because there is no such thing as targetting for a specific exchange rate in our policy," she said. \par \par \uc2  She also said the ministry was closely watching the movements of the won versus the dollar and the yen. Japan is the main competitor to South Korea in major export markets. \par \par \uc2  Regarding the local stock market's recent rally to nearly three-year highs, Kang said the government might decide to sell its holdings of shares in several local banks. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Selling the banking shares will be determined by the market condition," she said. "When the timing is right, depending on the KOSPI's\tab    movement, then the government will sell the banking shares."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked whether the government will be more tempted to sell the shares if the Korea Composite Stock Price Index (KOSPI) continues to rally strongly, Kang said: "Right".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But she denied that the share sale was designed to pull down the stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's wrong to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market," she said. "It's not necessarily for the purpose of moving around the KOSPI."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Seoul Newsroom +82 2 727 5646, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6b06l9k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal