\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA MARKETS - Investors sidelined by uncertainty. \b0\par\par\uc2 948 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1999\par 11:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 11 (Reuters) - Asian shares and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  were mixed on Friday, although Japan's euphoria over strong GDP \par \par \uc2  data lent some support. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar/yen\tab     volatility was seen limiting activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, as investors waited for it to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par settle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The dollar was still bearish against the yen by late trade,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par but dealers said caution over possible Bank of Japan (BOJ)\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was limiting dollar sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong shares\tab     firmed more than one percent, in\par line with Japan's benchmark Nikkei average\tab     , which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par finished 0.56 percent higher at 17,198.55.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SOUTH KOREAN SHARES AND WON CLOSE LOWER AFTER FLUCTUATIONS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     South Korea's won\tab     inched slightly lower against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar on Friday as a series of government measures erased\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earlier gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in shortly before the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par closing and bought about $100 million.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came after a comment by an IMF official who\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par told Reuters that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faced no restraints in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to smooth day-to-day volatility on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on each of the past two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par days, buying more than $100 million on Thursday and $50 million\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to $60 million on Wednesday, reflecting their concern that a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong won would hurt exports, thereby hindering a nascent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Andrew Dermot Fung, regional treasury economist at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Standard Chartered Bank in Singapore, said he thought the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was more worried with the pace of the won's rise,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rather than the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength itself.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's this really strong view that as the economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strengthens, so will the won, and inflows are gong to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par coming back as both Korea and the rest of the region improves,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "So it's not a case of Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the MOFE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Economy) standing in front of a train\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and saying stop. In fact it's more like them saying the pace is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a bit excessive, so we'll slow it down so that the impact on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports will be less," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korean shares closed lower after a MOFE spokeswoman\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par told Reuters Television that the stock market's further rally\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might lead the government to sell its shares of local commercial\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Selling the banking shares will be determined by the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par condition," spokeswoman Kang Yeoun-sun said. "When the timing is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par right, depending on the KOSPI's movement, then the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will sell the banking shares."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO CUT KEY OVERNIGHT RATES\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would cut its key\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overnight rates by 12.5 basis points each on Monday. The cuts\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would bring down the overnight borrowing rate to 9.5 percent and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the overnight lending to 11.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The move, aimed at spurring banks to lend and boost economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery, would be the 17th cut this year in overnight rates for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a total of 387.5 basis points.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR POSTS FOUR-MONTH HIGH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar\tab   posted its fifth consecutive gain,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par notching a four-month closing high as the weakening U.S. dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas showed few signs of a recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Turnover was active at $497.5 million on the main market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday that the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recent appreciation reflected international trends such as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in yen and other regionals. It also pledged to respect\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market forces.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH STEADY, TONE CAUTIOUS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Indonesian rupiah\tab   was steady in thin trade, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relief over the lack of election-related violence wearing as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attention moved to the slowness of vote-counting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par One foreign bank dealer said the rupiah was still cautious\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and would remain trading in a tight range, as uncertainty was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par considered too high by speculative players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Change on the day FRI 11 0918GMT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...Latest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ringgit......3.7995.......3.8000..........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rupiah......7670.00......7725.00..........0.72%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht..........36.91........36.91..........0.00%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Peso..........37.85........37.80........-0.13% Sing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dlr.....1.7134.......1.7135.........0.01% Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dlr...32.415.......32.420.........0.02% Korean\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won..1166.80......1166.00........-0.07% Japan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen....118.55.......119.28..