\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Holding up, marking time. \b0\par\par\uc2 995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1999\par 13:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 9 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held firm on Wednesday as the dollar steadied after big drops against the euro and yen, but the surge in U.S. long bond yields to a six percent high kept alive fears of a U.S. interest rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Major central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little moved after making substantial headway on Tuesday, although the Slovak crown was slightly weaker ahead of a 300 million euro bond issue expected later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were largely unchanged on late New York levels although at least two central banks, in Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , were reported to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains made on the back of the stronger yen. \par \par \uc2  The won earlier reached around 1,161 to the dollar and remained up on the day despite dollar buying by the Bank of Korea, traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to confirm the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar held around three-month highs against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the Indonesian rupiah, which surged on Monday and Tuesday on a wave of cheer over the peaceful turnout to the country's first real democratic elections in 44 years, shed some of its gloss, falling back through 7,700 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts said the slow pace of the vote count, which has prompted opposition parties to voice fears of possible tampering, was weighing on the market. \par \par \uc2  Others were more upbeat. \par \par \uc2  "This is just a cooling-off period - some reflection, some profit-taking," said Jake Moore, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  With less than four percent of votes counted by 0915 GMT, early results showed two major opposition parties had a strong lead over the ruling Golkar party. \par \par \uc2  "Near term, markets are likely to become more cautious as delays in vote counting and reporting will dampen sentiment," analysts at Standard Chartered said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/rupiah is expected to edge back towards 7,900 before a move to 7,500 is seen." \par \par \uc2  Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed no immediate reaction to a Chinese state radio report that the country was cutting its benchmark interest rate to 2.25 percent from 3.78 percent. \par \par \uc2  In Europe the Polish zloty, Czech crown and Hungarian forint barely budged. The forint remained at the top of its trading band, 2.25 percent above basket parity, while the zloty stuck around its four-week high of 2.86 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  The zloty faced tough resistance at three percent above the mid-point, but capital inflows from privatisations such as the $1 billion sale of Polish bank Pekao SA and higher growth expectations in Germany could lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The rand also held steady after the South African Reserve bank sanctioned a further small decline in its repo rate to 15.375 percent from 15.406 percent, bolstering hopes that commercial banks will soon ease their prime lending rates. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to ease further in the medium term, possibly towards 6.50 to the dollar by the end of the year, because of a continuing inflation differential between South Africa and the major industrial economies. \par \par \uc2  "It's slightly undervalued, but that undervaluation should probably persist because the latest figures show exports are not yet picking up," analyst Jean-Francois Mercier of Salomon Smith Barney told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the overnight rise in U.S. long bond yields increased nervousness over the possibility the U.S. Federal Reserve would raise interest rates later this month, which could squeeze capital flows to emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact would be seen mainly in Latin America later in the day, they added, as that region was likely to feel the greatest pinch from higher U.S. rates. \par \par \uc2  The Mexican peso, usually the only major Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade in the London morning, eased slightly from late New York levels. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Czech Rep.\tab \tab     37.28