\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won turns weaker by midday on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1999\par 05:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SEOUL, May 26 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's won\tab   stood turned weaker by midday on Wednesday after a state bank's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sparked dollar short-covering.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won ended the morning at 1,189.9 against Tuesday's 1,187.0 close. It opened at 1,186.0 and ranged from 1,184.3 to 1,193.0.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Export-Import Bank of Korea's bids had massed at the 1,190 won level, briefly pushing the dollar up to 1,193.0 won near the close of the morning. \par \par \uc2  "The bank is believed to have placed orders at up to the 1,192 won level but it's unclear whether the strong (dollar) sentiment could be sustained because there are many corporate sellers waiting there," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen\tab   extended its gains against the dollar but failed to provide a lasting lift to the won although the yen's strength overnight caused the won to open stronger.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen was quoted at 121.77/80 at midday, compared with 122.71/74 late on Tuesday in Tokyo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders showed no immediate reaction to the news that Korea Telecom Corp  raised $2.49 billion through an American Depositary Receipt sale.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government has said it would keep the proceeds from flowing into the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and finance ministry officials reaffirmed the stance on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said part of the money would be purchased by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Korea and that the remaining amount would be used by Korea Telecom's overseas \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Remarks by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor released early on Wednesday morning were generally ignored. Bank of Korea Governor Chon Chol-hwan said in a speech to a forum that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate should be left to market forces.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He reaffirmed the interest rate policy would continue to be geared towards supporting the economic recovery, indicating that there would be no swift rebound in local interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "A correlation between the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level and local interest rates is not apparent at the moment. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate should be decided by the market's supply and demand factors," Chon said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the non-deliverable forward trading, the six-month won was quoted at 1,194/97 at midday versus 1,191/94 in the morning and the one-year won stood at 1,200/03 versus 1,196.5/99.5.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Yoo Choon-sik, Seoul Newsroom +82 2 727 5646, fax +82 2 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv5q005x5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
