\par\par \b \uc2  ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Regionals lose early shine as yen dips. \b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1999\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      0900 GMT - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly lower in late \par \par \uc2  trading having lost an early firmer bias as the dollar picked \par \par \uc2  up to above the 115 level. \par \par \uc2      Dollar/yen recovered to its highest level since February 1 \par \par \uc2  after a Wall Street Journal article reported that the U.S. was \par \par \uc2  urging Japan to ease monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      Among the regionals the rupiah and peso bucked the trend. \par \par \uc2      *** The rupiah moved up after comments from both IMF's Asia \par \par \uc2  Pacific Director Hubert Neiss and Indonesia's own Minister of \par \par \uc2  Industry and Trade Rahardi Ramelan, although it failed to break \par \par \uc2  the 8,500 level. \par \par \uc2  Both officials said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could appreciate further \par \par \uc2  while the Trade Minister said it may head toward 7,500 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar, although he added that strength beyond 7,000 is \par \par \uc2  undesirable due to an impact on exports. \par \par \uc2      Hopes for the next IMF disbursement and talk of a possible \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support also gave the rupiah a lift. \par \par \uc2      *** In Manila, the peso rebounded on a surge in corporate \par \par \uc2  demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Traders said some of the corporate inflows could have come \par \par \uc2  from the San Miguel/Nestle deal. \par \par \uc2      Around $300 million in inflows were expected from the sale \par \par \uc2  of San Miguel's stake in Nestle Philippines. Those gains \par \par \uc2  completely wiped out earlier fears of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  *** The Thai baht was little changed. Hopes of a possible \par \par \uc2  easing of reserve requirements were dashed after the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Thailand announced that it had not discuss such a plan in a \par \par \uc2  meeting with commercial banks earlier today. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it wanted to see lower lending \par \par \uc2  rates although it would leave market forces to determine those \par \par \uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2      *** In Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there was talk of government \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar was little changed when the central back \par \par \uc2  stepped in to prop up the market and stop further losses. \par \par \uc2      Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to boost market \par \par \uc2  confidence, after poor economic growth figures on Monday. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, dealers say persistent dollar buying by Korean \par \par \uc2  state banks failed to keep the won from sliding. \par \par \uc2  - Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Desk (65) 870-3840 \par \par \uc2  - Email: asia.\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 @reuters.com \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab  ..Latest bid....Prev Close....Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Ringgit......3.7998.......3.8000..........0.01%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Rupiah......8600.00......8700.00..........1.16%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Baht..........37.02........37.00.........-0.05%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Peso..........38.95........39.40..........1.16%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sing dlr.....1.6935.......1.6920.........-0.09%\p