\par\par \b \uc2  SKorea won opens lower on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , KAMCO talk. \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 1998\par 02:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won opened weaker on Wednesday on market talk that local banks were stocking up on dollars to accommodate the sale of their non-performing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets to a government agency, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won opened at 1215.0 per dollar against Tuesday's 1,211.5 close. \par \par \uc2  "Aside from the KAMCO rumours, traders remain wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at HSBC Bank. \par \par \uc2  State-run Korea Asset Management Corp (KAMCO) earlier this year agreed to purchase in won some non-performing foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets from local banks. \par \par \uc2  "Rumours that the purchases would begin before the end of this year are gaining credibility," said a foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said banks would need to buy dollars on the inter-bank market to accommodate the asset sales. They said the demand would reach some $700 million to $800 million. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the won was expected to be bound within the 1,205 to 1,215 range in the absence of new factors affecting the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They noted the Japanese yen, which usually underpins the won's movement, remained almost unchanged from its previous close in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  The yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 116.73/83 per dollar in Tokyo versus an overnight close of 116.50/60 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The market would not likely be affected by an expected announcement on Wednesday of deals between local conglomerates and their creditor banks as part of a credit-for-restructuring plan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ((Nick Yon, Seoul newsroom, +822 727 5644, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  Trading in the won was expected to be bound within the 1,205 to 1,215 range in the absence of new factors affecting the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They noted the Japanese yen, which usually underpins the won's movement, remained almost unchanged from its previous close in overnight trading. \par \par \uc2  The yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 116.73/83 per dollar in Tokyo versus an overnight close of 116.50/60 in New York. \par \par \uc2  The market would not likely be affected by an expected announcement on Wednesday of deals between local conglomerates and their creditor banks as part of a credit-for-restructuring plan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  ((Nick Yon, Seoul newsroom, +822 727 5644, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926ducg02emw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
