\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won ends stronger amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 408 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 1998\par 09:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The South Korean won closed stronger against the dollar on Monday but its upside remained limited because of persistent concerns the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might step into the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said a new credit rating assignment by Moody's Investors Service on won-denominated state bonds provided a psychological boost to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The won closed at 1,208.0, compared with Friday's finish of 1,214.0. After opening at 1,210.0, it moved in a 1,211.0-1,204.0 range. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar has continued to fall by 10 won every day," said a foreign bank dealer. "But \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears and the yen/dollar movement erased early losses." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was slightly higher against the yen in late Tokyo but operators were reluctant to buy dollars aggressively as the U.S. unit failed to recover convincingly last Friday despite stronger-than-expected U.S. payroll data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the dollar slipped as low as 118.23 yen but rebounded to 118.86/96 at 0614 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer said many believed the dollar looked cheap versus the won but have hesitated to actively buy dollars, given the persistent supply of the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market hailed the Moody's decision as it was believed to be the first step before upgrading South Korea's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated sovereign bonds. \par \par \uc2  Moody's Investors Service assigned a Baa1 rating to the won-denominated bonds of South Korea. Baa1 is two notches above the lowest investment grade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said aggressive foreign buying in the local stock market, bolstered by Moody's rating announcement, would provide a stimulus to prop up the won against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The stock market soared by more than four percent with foreign net buying amounting to 30.67 billion won worth. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said market attention focused on whether the 1,200 won support level would be breached. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is likely to touch 1,180 won this week," said the local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said concerns about export growth, the key factor to boost \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economoy, would invite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and limit any freefall on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting cautiousness, trading volume remained weak at $477.2 million. ((Yeom Yoon-jeong, Seoul Newsroom +822 727 5647, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926duc702xci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
