\par\par \b \uc2  SKorea won opens up on expected mth-end dlr supply. \b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1998\par 03:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 29 (Reuters) - South Korea's won opened stronger against the dollar on Wednesday on an expected rise in exporter dollar sales towards the month-end, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The won was traded at 1,239 per dollar at 0058 GMT after opening at 1,245, against Tuesday's 1,257 finish. \par \par \uc2  "Traders think the market overreacted (to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments) yesterday when exporter negotiations are set to rise towards the month-end," said a Boston Bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The won tumbled nearly six percent from its intraday peak on Tuesday after an International Monetary Fund official said a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's Asia-Pacific department director Hubert Neiss told Reuters Television on Tuesday there now was scope for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. ((Yoo Choon-sik, +822 727 5646, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010924du7t01aqi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
