\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Korea won takes U-turn on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoo Choon-sik \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1998\par 11:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won on Tuesday ended a rally which had lasted several weeks amid a flurry of rumours a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was imminent to boost the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The won finished at 1,257 per dollar, about six percent off the year high of 1,185 reached in the morning, after the dollar gained support from bargain hunting and short-covering. \par \par \uc2  The closing rate was also down from Monday's 1,209 close. \par \par \uc2  "Strong bargain hunting and short-covering bids emerged after comments by an IMF official about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on the belief that the dollar has hit its bottom," said a Korea Exchange Bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Rumours of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were already circulating but got a critical boost when a senior International Monetary Fund official said outright an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  IMF Asia-Pacific Department Director Hubert Neiss told Reuters Television there now was scope for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  He said with \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rebuilt to about $36 billion, "there is a possibility of careful, judicious (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least to smooth out day-to-day erratic movements". \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  situation in South Korea had made rapid progress, adding: "Indeed, the exchange rate has appreciated at a pace that has now raised concern." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears would keep discouraging dollar sellers for the time being but forecast the dollar's upside would be limited by still heavy dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  "Many people still think the dollar's downward trend will not easily change unless the market's heavy dollar positions become lighter," said a Korea Exchange Bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The won's year high of 1,185 reached on Tuesday represented a 68 percent gain in its value against the dollar since the won hit a record low of 1,995 in late December. \par \par \uc2  South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to only about $8.87 billion by the end of last year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed in its bid to defend its plunging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Then came the IMF, which in December arranged a record-breaking $58.35 billion rescue package for what was the world's 11th-largest economy. \par \par \uc2  Together with aid loan payouts, rising current account surpluses and extension of maturities on South Korean financial institutions' short-term debt owed to international lenders also helped South Korea rebuild its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves \par \par \uc2  Active asset sales by South Korean companies to foreigners and a $4 billion overseas sovereign bond issue have also brought a flood of dollars into what was a dollar-hungry market. \par \par \uc2  South Korea said earlier on Tuesday it had agreed with the IMF to raise the usable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves forecast to $43 billion at the end of this year from $41 billion. \par \par \uc2  The won's sharp appreciation, also attributed to an extremely low dollar demand in line with plunging imports, is of particular concern to exporters. \par \par \uc2  A stronger won would make South Korean exports more expensive even without changes in won prices, depriving their products of comparative price competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  The won's appreciation was also in contrast with the weakening value of Japan's yen and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other South Korean competitors in exports against the dollar. ((Seoul Newsroom, +822 727 5646, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7s002jg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
