\par\par \b \uc2  S.Korea won closes lower. \b0\par\par\uc2 173 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juli 1998\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  "Strong bargain hunting and short-covering bids emerged after comments by an IMF official about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on the belief the dollar has hit its bottom," said a Korea Exchange Bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Talks of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were already circulating but got a critical boost when a senior International Monetary Fund official said outright an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible. \par \par \uc2  The IMF's Asia-Pacific department director Hubert Neiss told Reuters Television that there now was scope for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  He said with \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rebuilt to about $36 billion, "there is a possibility of careful, judicious (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , at least to smooth out day-to-day erratic movements". \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears would keep discouraging dollar sellers for the time being but forecast the dollar's upside would be limited by still heavy dollar positions. ((Yoo Choon-sik, +822 727 5646, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7s00279\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
