\par\par \b \uc2  PRESS DIGEST - South Korean newspapers - July 27. \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 1998\par 02:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  The following is a summary of major stories in leading South Korean newspapers, prepared by Reuters in Seoul. Reuters has not checked the stories and does not guarantee their accuracy. \par \par \uc2  Telephone: (822) 727-5644, Fax: (822) 727-5666 \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  MAEIL BUSINESS NEWSPAPER \par \par \uc2  - Interest rates for fixed deposits, repurchase agreements and certificates of deposit have decreased to 11 percent annually, said an official of the financial industry on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Korea will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize the won. The Bank of Korea said it will buy up the $270 million the Korea Exchange Bank is scheduled to bring in from its German investor, Commerzbank, early this week. \par \par \uc2  - When local financial firms close down, the South Korean government will ask foreign banks to extend interest rates and maturity for debts, said a government official. \par \par \uc2  - U.S.-based auto parts firm Delphi Co is seeking cooperation with South Korea's Mando Machinery, said an official from Delphi. \par \par \uc2  - Interest rates for KEPCO's samurai bonds of 10 billion yen or more will be 5.93 percent. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE KOREA ECONOMIC DAILY \par \par \uc2  - Representatives of some 100 South Korean firms will visit North Korea to attend the second investor relations sessions for Rajin-Sonbong free trade zone on September 24, said a South Korean government official on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - South Korean firms ranking six to 30 will get 1.3 trillion won in support for trade financing, said Park Tae-young, minister of industry and energy, on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE SEOUL ECONOMIC DAILY \par \par \uc2  - The South Korean government is seeking to develop a tourism programme which extends from North Korea's Paekdu Mountain to the far south Cheju Island, according to a government document found on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE DONG-A ILBO \par \par \uc2  - The South Korean government is seeking ways to improve relations with North Korea as soon as Kim Jong-il is expected to be inaugurated as state president possibly around September, said a senior official of the South Korean government on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - The South Korean government and business leaders agreed to pursue business exchanges, or "big deals", among the top five corporations. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE JOONGANG ILBO \par \par \uc2  - The Financial Supervisory Commission cancelled its plan to seek business exchanges among top five groups through local banks, said a commission official on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE KOREA TIMES \par \par \uc2  - The issuance of new shares worth hundreds of billions of won by Samsung Electronics and Samsung Electro-Mechanics is apparently aimed at raising the funds necessary to take over Kia Motors, in the event that Samsung's bid succeeds. \par \par \uc2  - \par \par \uc2  THE KOREA HERALD \par \par \uc2  - Less than 30 years after its founding, Korea Trading International Inc, a foreign trader on behalf of numerous small businesses, must decide whether or not to go on in the face of snowballing losses, sources said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7r007hg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
