\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-S.Korea minister warns of  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoo Choon-sik \par \uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1998\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SEOUL, July 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister on Thursday said the government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the won from becoming overvalued against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The government is closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with concern and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market is in serious problems," Finance and Economy Minister Lee Kyu-sung told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Lee was speaking after the won gained more than 50 percent against the dollar since hitting a record low of 1,995 in late December. \par \par \uc2  The surge has been underpinned by accumulating current account surpluses. Dollars have streamed into the country with disbursements from an international aid package, a $4 billion overseas sovereign bond issue and a spate of major asset sales to foreigners by indebted Korean companies. \par \par \uc2  The extension of maturities on nearly $22 billion in short-term debt by international banks in March has also considerably eased the demand for dollars in the local market, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Lee's comment immediately sent the won retreating to a midday close of 1,283 on Thursday, against Wednesday's 1,282 finish. It was far off from its session high of 1,265 which was also an intra-year high. \par \par \uc2  "The minister's remarks and some importer settlement bids boosted the dollar towards the morning close," said a dealer with a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  "But I expect the impact of the remarks to be short-lived unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actually steps in." \par \par \uc2  Lee also said the government would retain its "neither confirm nor deny" stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rumours. His remarks reversed comments made on Monday when he said there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  even if the won rose above 1,300. \par \par \uc2  He said it was not appropriate for the government to "give signals on every movement in the exchange rate", indicating that a lack of comment would not exclude the possibility of an immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upsurge has raised concerns the strong won could endanger the nation's efforts to overcome its worst economic crisis in decades through exports, because a stronger won would make the country's exports more expensive. \par \par \uc2  The won's strength is especially of big concern, as the Japanese yen has weakened against the dollar this year. South Korea and Japan compete in major export markets for products ranging from electronic goods to automobiles and ships. \par \par \uc2  The financial crisis forced South Korea to accept a rescue package of $58.35 billion from the International Monetary Fund in December in exchange for painful economic reforms. ((Seoul Newsroom, +822 727 5646, fax +822 727 5666, seoul.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7g00sf3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
