\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging market  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  - Won, rupiah on skids again. \b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Sharp drops in the South Korean won and the Indonesian rupiah led emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on Tuesday despite some talk that the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in London. \par \par \uc2  Growing concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial woes and overnight rumours about President Suharto's health led to the steep declines in both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  One market specialist in London said the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up its ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but other dealers discounted the talk saying the rupiah showed no signs of recovery. \par \par \uc2  Both the won and the rupiah set new record lows as the Asian crisis showed no signs of abating. \par \par \uc2  The won plummeted to a new historic low of 1,465.7 per dollar bid, down from Monday's levels of 1,342.4 and the rupiah sank to a new record low in London of 4,640 to the dollar, from 4,156 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "Overnight rumours of Suharto's health pushed the rupiah down," said Gerry Celaya, senior director at American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "They were more or less dispelled by the government  but again the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has remained weak and it is still well above 4,500 so it's pretty much an overnight decline of nine percent," he added. \par \par \uc2  Bearish sentiment continued to drag down the Korean won as dealers questioned the credibility of the government and its commitment to implement reforms demanded by the International Monetary Fund (IMF) as part of its $57 billion rescue package. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean government is set to hold presidential elections on December 18. \par \par \uc2  The won was pulled even lower following news on Monday that Korea's useable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to just $6.0 billion on December 2 from $22.5 billion on October 31. \par \par \uc2  In the text of the IMF agreement distributed by the country's Finance Ministry earlier on Tuesday, the IMF said South Korea's policy response to rapid deterioration of its external financing situation at the end of October was "piecemeal" and it had waited until November 21 to approach the Fund. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the won to reach the 1,500  psychological level. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment it seems like it is very much a one way market," said Celaya. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is looking at 1,500 level as some sort of psychological resistance level and more or less the last barrier (before) 2,000 but I don't really think we will see it get there, but obviously that is the risk," he added. \par \par \uc2  The drop in the won and the rupiah weighed on other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pulling the Thai baht in offshore markets down to 42.65 from 41.50 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, analysts said emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held up rather well. \par \par \uc2  "Despite further deep uncertainty in emerging Asia, we actually see a much calmer environment in major east European countries," said David Simmons, head of research for central and eastern Europe at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "In particular, we continue to see dollar/rouble trading significantly stronger," he added. \par \par \uc2  EXCHANGE RATE MOVERS \par \par \uc2  ASIA \par \par \uc2  * South Korean won weakens to 1465.7 from 1342.4 per dollar bid. Indonesian rupiah  down to 4605 from Monday's 4,155 per dollar bid. \par \par \uc2  * Malaysia's ringgit at 3.6655 per dollar bid down from 3.6485. Offshore baht  at 42.65 per dollar bid from 41.5. \par \par \uc2  EUROPE \par \par \uc2  * Russian rouble unchanged at 5,916 per dollar from Monday's level. \par \par \uc2  * Czech little changed at 19.679 bid from 19.699. \par \par \uc2  * Polish zloty versus dollar at 3.544 versus Monday's levels of 3.554. \par \par \uc2  AFRICA \par \par \uc2  * South African rand  at 4.8689 per dollar bid from 4.865. \par \par \uc2  LATIN AMERICA \par \par \uc2  * Mexican peso at 8.11 bid. \par \par \uc2  ((Diane Craft, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5110, fax 583 7239, uk.emergingmarkets.news@reuters.com)) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtc901cpy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
